diff --git b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md a/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
index 08d53d4..00b4c5f 100644
--- b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
+++ a/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@ The table above is the short list. This part covers the remaining `MOE_CACHE_*`
 | `MOE_CACHE_LOOKAHEAD_GUESS` | With lookahead prefetch on, how many experts per layer are looked at when guessing what comes next. 0 (or less) means the number the model uses per token. Ignored unless `MOE_CACHE_LOOKAHEAD` is on. | 0 (the model's experts per token) | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_LOOKAHEAD_THREADS` | With lookahead prefetch on, the number of helper threads that read experts ahead. Clamped to 1..32. Ignored unless `MOE_CACHE_LOOKAHEAD` is on. | 4 | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_MODELS_JSON` | Path of a models list file to use instead of the bundled `models.json` in the repository root (the parent of `bin/`, not next to the launcher script). The code comment says it is for tests. | Unset or empty (the bundled `models.json`) | internal/testing |
+| `MOE_CACHE_PLAN_COST` | Any value other than empty or `0` turns on a planner change: from 64k context on, the planner no longer skips the larger batch size 2048 when the compute-buffer table has no measured row for it (it uses an estimate instead), because 2048 was fastest for very long prompts in the project's measurements. | Off | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_POOL_CLAIM` | How many work chunks each plugin worker thread grabs at a time from the shared queue. Clamped to 1..64. A non-number counts as 1. | 1 | internal/testing |
 | `MOE_CACHE_POOL_TINY` | When on, a job of a single chunk runs directly on the calling thread, with no wake-up of the worker threads. Set `0` (or `off`/`false`/`no`) to turn that shortcut off. | On | internal/testing |
 | `MOE_CACHE_PREFILL_LEND_MIB` | While a long prompt is processed, the expert cache gives this many MiB back to the system and takes them back when generation starts. Prints a message when it happens. | 0 (off) | advanced |
